NevilleB wrote:
> I had some games recently which had the following "rare" levels - I'm
> curious to hear about other rare experiences people have:
> 
> game 1: a shop on level 13 and level 14 and a aligned temple [altar +
> priest] on level 15
> game 2: a rare bookshop with maybe 25 spellbooks
> game 3: a bookshop with maybe 10 spellbooks and 50 or so scrolls
> game 4: jewellery shop with maybe 50 rings, a liquor emporium with
> maybe 60 potions, and a leprechaun hall with perhaps 50 leprechauns!

Well, you wrote you had games (plural!), so I think such observations
won't happen too rarely. In my own experience I had observed extreme
variances between different games; e.g. a game without any shops, and
the guaranteed ones in minetown in a quite minimal variant, where the
random shops haven't been generated; besides lighting just one more.
Then games without altars at all (besides the guaranteed ones), and
the guaranteed temple non co-aligned. On the other hand I had games
with altars on every other level, sometimes 3 or 4 on a single level,
including occasional temples of any alignment. For the large shops
to be generated there must be some coincidence in level generation
(AFAIK); first the level must be randomly layouted with large rooms,
then some random factor will determine whether a special room will
be generated (possible room types depending on dungeon level), and
finally the room must qualify for a special room (e.g. shops have one
entrance). So I'd say, those streaks of games are rare, but not too
exceptional.

